  data:  # 031b
    kind: invariant  # 031b
    title: "Entrypoint detection is Python-only: 0 of 64 entrypoints are bash/TS/JS/HTML scripts on hypergumbo self-analysis (entrypoints.py has no shebang/executable logic)"  # 031b
    status: violated  # 031b
    priority: 2  # 031b
    parent:  # 031b
    tags:  # 031b
    - analysis_quality  # 031b
    - dogfood_round19  # 031b
    - entrypoint_detection  # 031b
    isbefore: []  # 031b
    duplicate_of: []  # 031b
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 031b
    pr_ref:  # 031b
    description: "**Found via self-analysis dogfooding on 2026-05-17 (round 19, dead-code seed variation investigation).**\n\n**Symptom.** `hypergumbo`'s entrypoint detection is entirely Python-centric. On hypergumbo's own self-analysis:\n\n```python\nentrypoint kinds: main_function (17), library_export (39), http_route (8)  # total 64\nentrypoint languages: python (64), bash (0), typescript (0), javascript (0), html (0), shell (0)\n```\n\nThe repository has ~50 bash scripts (`scripts/release-check`, `scripts/auto-pr`, `scripts/ci-debug`, `.githooks/commit-msg`, etc.), several TS files (`packages/htrac-frontend/src/main.ts`, `vite.config.ts`), an `index.html`, and a service worker — NONE are detected as entrypoints.\n\n**Root cause.** `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/entrypoints.py` has zero mentions of `bash`, `shell`, `.sh`, `shebang`, or `executable`. The detection logic only recognizes:\n\n- `main_function` — Python `def main():` and `if __name__ == \"__main__\"` modules\n- `library_export` — Python `__all__` / exported symbols\n- `http_route` — framework-detected route handlers (FastAPI, Starlette, etc.)\n\nBash/shell scripts have no equivalent detection. A standalone executable script with `#!/usr/bin/env bash` is treated as \"interior\" code with no entry point — meaning ALL its helper functions look unreachable.\n\n**Downstream impact.**\n\n1. **`dead-code-maybe` FP inflation.** All 153 bash functions in the codebase look \"potentially dead\" because no bash module is in the entrypoint set. This is a primary driver of the 92.6% candidate rate observed in WI-vuton with `--seeds entrypoints` (the default).\n\n   Seed variation confirms this:\n   - `--seeds entrypoints` (default, 64 seeds): **92.6% dead** (3719/4016)\n   - `--seeds exports` (934 seeds): 55.0% dead (2207/4016)\n   - `--seeds tests` (19529 seeds): 41.4% dead (1661/4016)\n   - `--seeds all` (20492 seeds): 39.5% dead (1586/4016)\n   \n   The 53-point swing across seed types points to insufficient entrypoint detection rather than actual dead code.\n\n2. **Slice / reverse-slice from entrypoints.** A user running `hypergumbo slice --entry release-check` to trace what a script does cannot seed from the script module itself — the slice command would need a Python entrypoint to start.\n\n3. **io-boundaries reachability annotation.** I/O calls within bash scripts (e.g., `subprocess.run` inside `.githooks/commit-msg`) show as \"no reachable entrypoint\" even though the .git-hook itself is the entrypoint. Misleads `verify-claims` audits.\n\n4. **Other languages similarly affected.** htrac-frontend's `main.ts` (top-level script) is not an entrypoint; neither is `index.html`. SPA/Electron entrypoints have a parallel item INV-risag.\n\n**Fix proposal.**\n\nExtend entrypoint detection (entrypoints.py) with:\n1. **Bash/shell script detection.** Files with `#!/usr/bin/env bash` or `#!/bin/bash` or `#!/bin/sh` shebang lines, or files in conventional directories (`scripts/`, `.githooks/`, `bin/`) with executable permissions → emit `<module:foo>` as entrypoint with `kind=shell_script`.\n2. **HTML entry detection.** index.html → emit as entrypoint with `kind=html_entry` (also covers SPA root).\n3. **TS/JS standalone-script detection.** A .ts/.js file with top-level executable code (not just exports) and no inbound `imports` edges → emit as entrypoint with `kind=script_module`.\n\nRegression test: hypergumbo run on a small repo with one bash script and one Python file produces ≥2 entrypoints (one each).\n\n**Severity.** Medium — coverage gap that inflates dead-code FP rate, breaks slice traversal from non-Python scripts, and underspecifies io-boundaries reachability.\n\n**Cross-references.**\n- WI-vuton (dead-code-maybe systematic FPs on polymorphic dispatch — 92.6% candidate rate) — this finding is a SECOND cause of that 92.6% rate, complementing the polymorphic-dispatch story.\n- WI-pulor (bash analyzer: lines_of_code=None, no intra-script edges) — the intra-script-edges claim is wrong (211 intra-script bash edges exist on May 17); the LOC=None claim is still correct (153/153 bash functions have lines_of_code=None despite span being populated). Discussion note added.\n- INV-hosuh (entrypoint double-counting __main__ + main()) — adjacent on entrypoint-detection axis.\n- INV-risag (SPA/Electron entrypoint must be detected) — adjacent (TS/JS entry, currently `holding` P1).\n- INV-lumiz (Java/C#/Kotlin main() detection broken) — another instance of language-coverage gap.\n\n**Notebook reference.** `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_05162026_0438.md` Round 19 section."  # 031b
    fields:  # 031b
      statement: "Entrypoint detection must recognize executable scripts in any language hypergumbo supports, not just Python. Currently entrypoints.py only emits main_function (Python def main()), library_export (Python __all__), and http_route (Python framework routes). On hypergumbo's self-analysis: 64 entrypoints, 100% Python, ZERO bash/TS/JS/HTML. The repo has ~50 bash scripts + 7+ TS files + HTML + service worker that are all real entry points but get no recognition."  # 031b
      root_cause: "entrypoints.py has no code paths for shebang detection (#!/usr/bin/env bash), executable-permission detection, or conventional-directory heuristics (scripts/, .githooks/, bin/). It also has no HTML entry-point or TS/JS standalone-script-module detection. The detection is keyed entirely on Python-specific patterns. Fix: add (a) shell_script entrypoint kind for shebang+executable files, (b) html_entry for index.html and similar SPA roots, (c) script_module for TS/JS files with top-level code and no inbound imports. Regression test: 2-file repo (one bash script, one Python file) produces ≥2 entrypoints. Downstream impact: dead-code-maybe FP rate (92.6%→39.5% across seed variation), slice traversal from scripts, io-boundaries reachability annotation."  # 031b
